  "articleBody": "Thinking about finishing your basement? That's awesome! It can add so much value and usable space to your home. But before you get started, there are some super important things to check off your list to make sure your project goes smoothly. First, and this is a big one, check for any signs of moisture. Are there water stains, damp spots, or a musty smell? If so, you've gotta fix that *before* anything else. Next, take a look at your foundation walls for any cracks or structural issues. It's much easier and cheaper to address these now than after you've built out the space. You'll also want to consider your layout. What do you want this space to be? A bedroom, a family room, an office? Think about where your plumbing and electrical will need to go. And don't forget to look into permits! Many basement finishing projects, especially if you're adding new plumbing or electrical, require them. A good contractor, like us, can help guide you through the permit process, ensuring everything is up to code. This upfront planning saves a ton of headaches later!",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}